    "Reversed rays, projected to their terminal vertex", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"bea5623f-044e-4083-992f-93f7e380c01d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "054bb14d-949f-4583-b180-6d7cae5f3274"], Cell[
    "InfraDisplacementBundle[g,r]", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "734a45e8-30f9-4e81-be63-263fd860dbff"], Cell["\<\
Pairs of vertices at distance r, projected to the first vertex\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"cc19a7ee-ba5d-464e-838f-fe4471966d05"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "2f7d79e2-f8df-47b5-af91-516237a7dd7a"], Cell[
    "InfraBundleMorphism", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2110355e-06c5-47bd-9612-a96235bc0073"], Cell["\<\
Particular endpoint, truncation and reversal maps between these models\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"e5d75232-d030-41a4-8474-f90c8a5bf9ef"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "bd9137d2-e65c-4b7f-b3f0-4167cabd603d"], Cell[
    "InfraFiberedSubstrate", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "79bf0a34-2c50-4c2c-b228-020dd7fe200a"], Cell["\<\
A finite catalogue of products, coverings, branched examples and geometric \
models\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"878ddbd8-2886-4f42-8d4f-c1fb785a2632"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"280bfa09-ef0c-4fd1-9fa5-\
df2f28a3eae8"],

Cell["\<\
The tangent and cotangent models use adjacency or equality at each position \
of a ray. The displacement model uses this rule on the two entries of a pair. \
Their vertical graphs and transverse multiplicities depend on the substrate. \
Materializing a construction gives an ordinary literal fibered graph for the \
general readers. Supported models also have explicit predicate methods that \
materialize once, so manual conversion is optional.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eae820ee-dfd6-40dd-b3f6-f265858021e4"],

Cell["\<\
The same cycle supports two ray models and a displacement model.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5a80e4fa-3b1f-4346-b16b-a851989370fa"],

